WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:04.779
Would you eat a hamburger or a chicken nugget
made of meat grown in a laboratory?

00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:09.680
Joshua Tetrick, co-founder and CEO of JUST
is betting that you will.

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:15.780
In tomorrow's world, you can eat more meat,
hopefully safer meat, even better tasting meat,

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:17.680
without eating the animal.

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:19.860
JUST, which is based in San Francisco,

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:26.240
has been producing and selling non animal
versions of food like mayonnaise since 2013

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:30.960
and it's raised more than 310 million dollars
in venture capital.

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:34.359
Tetrick and his team have created products
like JUST Mayo

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:39.820
by identifying plant based alternatives to
common animal products like eggs.

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:45.540
We're one part pharma, one part bio-tech and
a whole bunch of regular food company.

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:48.800
We built a discovery system that has the only
patent in the world

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:51.700
that utilizes machine learning for food ingredient
discovery

00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:56.880
and it helped us find this mung bean that
when you put it in a pan scrambles

00:00:56.880 --> 00:01:01.360
and that process broken down means that we
source from over 51 countries in the world,

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:04.400
we look at about 21 different molecular properties,

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:08.880
we look at how that bean functions, does it
bake a cake, does it gel in a pan

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:11.980
and then we see if it makes ice cream or butter
or scrambled eggs.

00:01:11.980 --> 00:01:17.960
Our process of finding these new tools is
high tech, but what we find is not high tech at all.

00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:21.320
The mung bean has been in the world's food
system for 4400 years.

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:23.100
I sure as hell didn't invent the mung bean.

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:28.760
JUST is one of a handful of tech companies
working to disrupt the meat production industry.

00:01:28.760 --> 00:01:33.280
While many of it's competitors are pursuing
better plant based meat substitutes,

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:38.960
JUST is pushing ahead with so called clean
meat or lab grown animal tissue

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:43.860
that requires no farming, no feeding of livestock
and no slaughterhouses.

00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:48.880
Only a single sample from a single animal
duplicated endlessly.

00:01:48.890 --> 00:01:53.740
JUST and companies like it are poised to disrupt
the entire livestock industry

00:01:53.740 --> 00:01:58.120
but the established players are turning to
the government to protect their turf.

00:01:58.120 --> 00:02:02.940
The United States Cattlemen's Association,
which declined to participate in this story,

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:07.899
submitted a petition still under consideration
by the United States Department of Agriculture

00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:11.840
asking that the words meat and beef exclude
any products

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:16.280
that are 'neither derived from animals, nor slaughtered
in the traditional manner.'

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:20.340
The power of the terms is a lot more powerful
than people think, especially in food.

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:26.470
Imagine Tesla launches a pickup truck, but
US Department of Transportation says

00:02:26.470 --> 00:02:29.870
'Hold up, Tesla, Elon, you can't call it a
pickup truck.'

00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:33.440
You have to call it electric mobility transport
unit.

00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:36.700
That's not winning in Alabama, even though
it might be fast,

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:39.520
even though it might have an amazing amount
of horsepower,

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:43.520
because a car is identity, but food's identity
even more.

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:48.840
JUST is also looking to transcend the vegan
vs carnivore paradigm.

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:51.340
We don't allow the term vegan to be used in
our company.

00:02:51.340 --> 00:02:54.200
Not because we don't believe in the spirit
of it,

00:02:54.200 --> 00:03:00.200
that word ends up turning off 99% of people.

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:02.140
The food system needs to start over,

00:03:02.140 --> 00:03:06.040
little girls in the second row of a class
in Liberia aren't getting proper nutrients,

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:12.800
a young boy growing up in Birmingham Alabama
is accelerating a path to Type 2 diabetes,

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:15.340
animals are being confined in needless ways,

00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:17.100
it's contributing to climate change,

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:19.460
and I think if we can think differently about
the food system

00:03:19.460 --> 00:03:22.660
while also realizing that we can't be so new
and so out there

00:03:22.660 --> 00:03:27.100
that it doesn't relate to the everyday human
being, we can do a whole lot of good.

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:28.560
And that's what I want to do.

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:32.740
This isn't Tetrick's first fight with entrenched
food interests.

00:03:32.740 --> 00:03:38.400
JUST Mayo has been threatened by the Egg Board,
I can't believe this.

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:43.740
When the company's first product, JUST Mayo,
appeared on the shelves of major retailers

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:46.960
the American Egg Board went on the attack.

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:50.400
It tried and failed to get Whole Foods to
pull the product from it's shelves

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:54.920
and hired a network of writers to trash the
product on food review sites.

00:03:54.920 --> 00:04:00.180
Target pulled JUST Mayo off it's shelves after
receiving an anonymous letter about food safety

00:04:00.180 --> 00:04:04.400
but an FDA investigation later found that
the product was safe.

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:08.000
And investigators failed to ever identify
the author of the letter.

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:12.920
At one point Egg Board members even discussed
putting out a hit on Tetrick

00:04:12.920 --> 00:04:17.400
with one writing that he should have his old
buddies from Brooklyn pay him a visit.

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:19.500
The officials claimed to be joking.

00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:23.580
I think the email where they discussed putting
a hit out on me,

00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:28.520
where the American Egg Board discusses that
was probably the most surprising.

00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:31.211
I mean, hell, at the time we probably had
15-20 people in the company

00:04:31.220 --> 00:04:32.500
I really didn't know what the hell I was doing.

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:36.960
And all of a sudden the egg industry has an
interest in this little mayo product.

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:40.080
And when bigger more entrenched folks pay
attention,

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:43.180
maybe it's validating that you're on to something.

00:04:43.180 --> 00:04:47.420
Whether or not consumers are ready for lab
grown meat is yet to be seen.

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:52.000
And the company landed in hot water with the
SEC in 2016

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:55.080
after being accused of buying it's own products
off the shelves

00:04:55.080 --> 00:04:57.840
to boost sales figures to raise more venture
capital.

00:04:57.840 --> 00:05:00.620
Though the company claims it was a quality
control measure

00:05:00.620 --> 00:05:03.440
and no charges resulted in the investigation.

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:06.860
But with JUST products in more than 20,000
stores

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:11.360
and plans to release lab grown clean meat
onto the market by the end of the year

00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:15.420
at a retail price within 30% of that of traditional
meat

00:05:15.420 --> 00:05:20.300
Tetrick is optimistic about the future of
his company and the global food system.

00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:25.840
It was an out of body experience to sit there
and eat a chicken

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:31.780
but have the chicken that you're eating running
around in front of you.

00:05:31.780 --> 00:05:34.990
We're working on chicken nuggets, maybe fois
gras.

00:05:34.990 --> 00:05:41.300
I want to focus less on changing the cultural
and societal perceptions of a word,

00:05:41.300 --> 00:05:43.080
I don't know how long that's gonna take,

00:05:43.080 --> 00:05:47.260
and more on feed as many people as I can
every day a little bit better.

